================================================================================================
S596  rigidity = orbit-type; the 2-adic seam unifies the apex, the doubling collapse
================================================================================================

[1] THE REFLECTION <-1>: apex = the second fixed point n/2, exists IFF n even
  n | fixed pts of x->-x | #±-pairs | apex present?
   3 | [0]            |       1  | no
   4 | [0, 2]         |       1  | YES (apex=2)
   5 | [0]            |       2  | no
   6 | [0, 3]         |       2  | YES (apex=3)
   7 | [0]            |       3  | no
   8 | [0, 4]         |       3  | YES (apex=4)
   9 | [0]            |       4  | no
  10 | [0, 5]         |       4  | YES (apex=5)
  11 | [0]            |       5  | no
  12 | [0, 6]         |       5  | YES (apex=6)
  13 | [0]            |       6  | no
  14 | [0, 7]         |       6  | YES (apex=7)
  15 | [0]            |       7  | no
  16 | [0, 8]         |       7  | YES (apex=8)
  17 | [0]            |       8  | no
  18 | [0, 9]         |       8  | YES (apex=9)

[2] THE DOUBLING <2>: permutation (odd) vs 2-adic collapse (even); mixing if 2 prim root
  n | n factored | doubling perm? | 2 prim root? | <2>-orbit sizes on units
   3 | 3        | True           | True         | [2]
   4 | 2^2      | False          | False        | ['2-ADIC COLLAPSE']
