[3] THE FRONTIER as orbit-degeneracy: classify n by (v2, odd-part-type)
  n | v2(n) | class | LRC reading
   5 |    0  | ODD: 2-prim-root MAX-MIXING (easiest)
   7 |    0  | ODD: <2> splits (cyclotomic cosets)
   8 |    3  | 2^3·1: deep 2-adic seam
  10 |    1  | 2·prime: APEX + single 2-collapse = HARD FRONTIER
  11 |    0  | ODD: 2-prim-root MAX-MIXING (easiest)
  13 |    0  | ODD: 2-prim-root MAX-MIXING (easiest)
  14 |    1  | 2·prime: APEX + single 2-collapse = HARD FRONTIER
  16 |    4  | 2^4·1: deep 2-adic seam
  17 |    0  | ODD: <2> splits (cyclotomic cosets)
  18 |    1  | 2^1·9: deep 2-adic seam
  22 |    1  | 2·prime: APEX + single 2-collapse = HARD FRONTIER
  23 |    0  | ODD: <2> splits (cyclotomic cosets)

